Fall back to the registered fonts before the system's, in the nearest weight

Compose registers the fonts an app loads (and any fallbacks it adds) with a TypefaceFontProviderWithFallback,
which FontMgrWithFallback asks only once the system's font manager has no font for a character. On a Mac,
CoreText always has one (Apple Color Emoji, PingFang, Hiragino), so text in an app's own font draws its emoji
and CJK from the machine, never from the fonts the app carries. This asks the registered fonts first, and the
system only for what none of them has.

Among the registered fonts that have the character, it takes the first one's family in the face nearest the
run's style, so a bold run falls back to a bold face rather than to whichever weight was registered first.

